id: pm-l6wdvh
title: "Shorten module-private identifiers in the unbundled runtime modules, restoring 1.76 MB of publication headroom"
description: "The packed distribution stood at 19,985,525 of 20,000,000 B after PR 1764, so the next SDK change could not ship. Build finalization compacted the 714 tsc-emitted modules outside dist/cli-bundle with identifier shortening off, although the CLI bundle built from the same sources has always shortened them. Turn it on, keep export names, module paths, declarations and source-map names, and keep repeated builds byte-stable."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: "area:release",distribution,packaging,performance
created_at: "2026-11-22T02:21:01.211Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-22T13:15:14.774Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
claim_principal: "harness:claude-code#8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "The packed distribution is at least 1.5 MB below the 20,000,000 B base ceiling on a clean build; Export names, module paths and declarations are unchanged and composed source maps keep original names, proven by the runtime compaction spec; A repeated finalization leaves an unchanged output and its source map byte-identical; The packed npx and bunx smoke passes"
parent: pm-998juj
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: "The packed distribution stays under the 20 MB publication ceiling with at least 1.5 MB of headroom, and repeated or interrupted builds emit the bytes a clean build emits"
