comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-22T02:21:01.211Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: pm search for runtime compaction and identifier minification returned the closed whitespace tranche pm-fx0rcb, which deliberately left identifiers alone, and no open item for identifier shortening. Filed as the closeable tranche child of the publication-weight owner."
  "2026-11-22T03:03:51.464Z","harness:claude-code","First Codex review finding: the first incremental build after switching from a tree built by the previous finalizer has no ledger, so already compacted outputs would be compacted again and differ from a clean build. scripts/prepare-build-cache.mjs now treats dist/.runtime-compaction.json as a required output: when it is missing, the TypeScript build cache is dropped and the compiler re-emits raw output for the finalizer."
  "2026-11-22T03:21:46.039Z","harness:claude-code","Second Codex round: an interrupted finalizer could leave a truncated ledger that the next build reads as empty while tsc reuses compacted outputs. The ledger is now written to a temporary file and published by rename, so an interruption leaves the previous ledger or none. Validating the ledger's JSON in prepare-build-cache was not added: with an atomic publish a truncated ledger cannot arise from an interrupted build."
  "2026-11-22T09:29:03.889Z","harness:claude-code","Review round on head 7e0844634 (Greptile P2, scripts/finalize-build.mjs). A build stopped after esbuild overwrote modules and before the new ledger was renamed left the previous ledger in place; the retry kept the TypeScript cache, saw digests that differed from the old ledger, and shortened already-shortened modules again. compactRuntimeOutputs now removes the ledger before it overwrites the first module, so an interrupted finalization leaves no ledger and prepare-build-cache discards the compiler cache, giving the finalizer raw output. Spec: runtime-compaction.spec.ts drives a failing finalization and asserts the ledger is absent afterwards.\n"
  "2026-11-22T13:15:14.774Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit round on head 42fa849f4. (1) scripts/prepare-build-cache.mjs now verifies every digest the ledger records against dist before the compile; a changed or missing output (source-map injection through sentry:inject, a stopped build) drops the ledger and the TypeScript cache, so the finalizer compacts raw output and never shortens an injected module again. Spec in prepare-build-cache.spec.ts on a real temp tree.\n"
